* **1 kHz LED PWM (TIM2 / PA0)**: TIM2 is clocked at $170\text{ MHz}$. With $\text{PSC} = 169$, the counter runs at $1\text{ MHz}$ ($1\text{ }\mu\text{s}$ per tick). An $\text{ARR} = 999$ produces a period of $1000\text{ }\mu\text{s}$ ($1\text{ kHz}$), and $\text{CCR1} = 500$ delivers a precise $50.0\%$ duty cycle.
* **50 Hz Servo Signal (TIM3 / PA6)**: A standard RC servo operates on a $20\text{ ms}$ ($50\text{ Hz}$) period with pulse widths from $1.0\text{ ms}$ to $2.0\text{ ms}$. TIM3 uses the same $1\text{ MHz}$ prescaler ($\text{PSC} = 169$), giving $\text{ARR} = 19999$ ($20\text{ ms}$). $\text{CCR1} = 1500$ sets the pulse width to $1.5\text{ ms}$ (neutral center position).
* **Timers**: Both TIM2 and TIM3 are general-purpose timers on APB1 and do not require break/dead-time main output enable (`BDTR_MOE`). Preload registers (`ARPE`, `OC1PE`) ensure glitch-free updates.

