- Assigned `AF2` in `GPIOB->AFR[0]` (`AFRL` bits `[19:16]`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.359].

#### 2. Timer Calculation (1 kHz, 50% Duty Cycle)
- **Timer Input Clock ($f_{\text{TIM}}$)**:
  - When the APB prescaler is 1, the timer clock frequencies (`tim_ker_ck`) are set to the same frequency of the APB domain ($f_{\text{TIM}} = 170\text{ MHz}$) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.281].
- **Prescaler ($PSC$) and Auto-Reload ($ARR$)**:
  $$f_{\text{PWM}} = \frac{f_{\text{TIM}}}{(PSC + 1) \times (ARR + 1)}$$
  Choosing $PSC = 3$ divides the timer clock by 4:
  $$f_{\text{CNT}} = \frac{170\text{ MHz}}{4} = 42.5\text{ MHz}$$
  To obtain $f_{\text{PWM}} = 1000\text{ Hz}$:
  $$ARR + 1 = \frac{42.5\text{ MHz}}{1000\text{ Hz}} = 42500 \implies ARR = 42499$$
  Resulting PWM frequency:
  $$f_{\text{actual}} = \frac{170{,}000{,}000}{(3 + 1) \times (42499 + 1)} = 1000.00\text{ Hz}\quad (0.00\%\text{ error})$$
- **Capture/Compare Register ($CCR1$)**:
  For edge-aligned PWM mode 1 (up-counting), the output is active while $\text{CNT} < CCR1$:
  $$\text{Duty Cycle} = \frac{CCR1}{ARR + 1} \times 100\% = 50\%$$
  $$CCR1 = \frac{42500}{2} = 21250\quad (50.00\%\text{ duty cycle})$$

