### I2C2 Configuration for 1.8 V Pressure Sensor

#### 1. Hardware & Resource Conflict Analysis
- **Pin Mapping & Conflict Resolution**:
  - In Message 2, PA9 was allocated to `USART1_TX` (AF7).
  - In Message 3, PA9 is requested for `I2C2_SCL` (AF4) and PA8 for `I2C2_SDA` (AF4) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73].
  - Because an MCU pin cannot drive both USART1 TX and I2C2 SCL simultaneously, USART1 was remapped to its standard alternate pins **PB6 (TX)** and **PB7 (RX)** on AF7 [STM32G474_Datasheet p.74], freeing PA9 for `I2C2_SCL` and allowing PA8 to serve as `I2C2_SDA`.
- **Electrical & Logic Level Compatibility**:
  - The STM32G474 operates at $V_{DD} = 3.3\text{ V}$. For all FT/standard I/O pins, the minimum input high voltage is $V_{IH,\min} = 0.7 \times V_{DD} = 2.31\text{ V}$ [STM32G474_Datasheet p.128].
