  - An open-drain bidirectional level shifter (such as a TXS0102 or discrete MOSFET circuit) between the 3.3 V domain (STM32 side, PA8/PA9) and the 1.8 V domain (sensor side) is necessary and satisfies all logic thresholds.

#### 2. Peripheral Clock & Timing Register Calculation
- `I2C2` is enabled on the APB1 bus via `RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_I2C2EN` [STM32G474_RM0440 p.309].
- By selecting `HSI16` (16 MHz) as the I2C2 kernel clock in `RCC->CCIPR` (`I2C2SEL = 0b10` at bits [15:14]) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.322], we obtain an exact, stable, standard-mode 100 kHz clock profile using the reference settings given in RM0440 Table 360 [STM32G474_RM0440 p.1657]:
  - `PRESC` = $3$ ($t_{\text{PRESC}} = (3 + 1) \times 62.5\text{ ns} = 250\text{ ns}$)
  - `SCLDEL` = $4$ ($t_{\text{SCLDEL}} = (4 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 1250\text{ ns}$)
  - `SDADEL` = $2$ ($t_{\text{SDADEL}} = 2 \times 250\text{ ns} = 500\text{ ns}$)
  - `SCLH` = $0x0F = 15$ ($t_{\text{SCLH}} = (15 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 4.0\ \mu\text{s}$)
  - `SCLL` = $0x13 = 19$ ($t_{\text{SCLL}} = (19 + 1) \times 250\text{ ns} = 5.0\ \mu\text{s}$)
  - Combined `I2C2->TIMINGR = 0x30420F13` produces standard-mode 100 kHz ($t_{SCL} \approx 10\ \mu\text{s}$).

#### 3. GPIO Configuration
- PA8 and PA9 are configured in Open-Drain Alternate Function mode:
  - `MODER8 = 0b10`, `MODER9 = 0b10` (Alternate Function mode) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.355].
  - `OTYPER8 = 1`, `OTYPER9 = 1` (Open-Drain output) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.356].
  - `PUPDR8 = 0b01`, `PUPDR9 = 0b01` (Internal pull-up enabled; external pull-ups to 3.3 V on the level shifter line are also present) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.356].
  - `AFR[1]` (AFRH): AF4 (`0b0100`) mapped to PA8 (`I2C2_SDA`) and PA9 (`I2C2_SCL`) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.73, RM0440 p.360].

